# UK design systems and Home Assistant controls

Use the GOV.UK foundations for clear structure, readable content and familiar form controls. Add a pattern from another official system only when it addresses the same user need. Preserve native Home Assistant capabilities, state meanings and accessible interactions where a public-service component does not describe the task.

This review maps the **38 documented Home Assistant families** (30 task specifications and 8 additional control/panel families) to specific official sources and local owners. It also records **365 direct catalogue entries across 17 indexes from 8 UK systems**. These counts describe reviewed information architecture and design decisions. They are not counts of new native adapters, installed packages or individually certified controls.

The [machine-readable crosswalk](../reference/uk-design-system-crosswalk.json) contains the exact source URLs, retrieval hashes, dates, existing local mappings and the decisions rendered below. The [component organisation review](component-audit.html) still owns shared component families and retained URLs. No existing guide is deprecated merely because another system uses a different name.

